invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: rsa_ifma_sign.c drops the target attribute that turns AVX-512F and
  AVX-512 IFMA on for its own functions, so the kernel compiles only where
  the whole object is built with those instructions, and an object built
  that way runs AVX-512 in code the caller's ch_cfg.cpu never chose. The
  script compiles the file for x86-64 with no instruction flag, as a host
  object compiles it, and the compile fails: each intrinsic needs a
  feature that only the attribute turned on.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx512f,avx512ifma"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("avx512f,avx512ifma")
#endif

#include "rsa_ifma_lanes.h"
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif

#include "rsa_ifma_lanes.h"
